From 3545285dd87dc654e84e62c21fa8b466417cca28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romeo Mattar <romeomat.work@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:09:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/ssi/esp32_spi: no command phase unless SPI_USR_COMMAND is
 set

A user transaction sends a command phase if SPI_USER.USR_COMMAND is set
or if SPI_USER2.USR_COMMAND_BITLEN is non-zero.  The TRM (v5.8, section
20.3) says each phase is enabled only by its control bit in SPI_USER,
and that the command bit length "is only valid when SPI_USR_COMMAND is
set to 1".

ESP-IDF's spi_master disables the command phase with usr_command = 0
and usr_command_bitlen = 0 - 1 (field value 15), so every transaction
clocked two extra bytes before the data; Arduino-ESP32 leaves the reset
value 4 and got one.  Every read from an SPI2/SPI3 device came back
shifted by one or two bytes.

Key the command phase on USR_COMMAND alone.  The SPI1 flash paths set
USR_COMMAND whenever they send a command; NVS and raw flash read, write
and erase still work.

Signed-off-by: Romeo Mattar <romeomat.work@gmail.com>
---
 hw/ssi/esp32_spi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/ssi/esp32_spi.c b/hw/ssi/esp32_spi.c
index f47bfca..4d0d12f 100644
--- a/hw/ssi/esp32_spi.c
+++ b/hw/ssi/esp32_spi.c
@@ -275,7 +275,7 @@ static void esp32_spi_do_command(Esp32SpiState* s, uint32_t cmd_reg)
 
     case R_SPI_CMD_USR_MASK:
         maybe_encrypt_data(s);
-        if (FIELD_EX32(s->user_reg, SPI_USER, COMMAND) || FIELD_EX32(s->user2_reg, SPI_USER2, COMMAND_BITLEN)) {
+        if (FIELD_EX32(s->user_reg, SPI_USER, COMMAND)) {
             t.cmd = FIELD_EX32(s->user2_reg, SPI_USER2, COMMAND_VALUE);
             t.cmd_bytes = bitlen_to_bytes(FIELD_EX32(s->user2_reg, SPI_USER2, COMMAND_BITLEN));
         } else {
